From 7e7600af120b0b5b16dc2346b264fb748b9d4bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:35:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] badgeui: a full action set per card type, and Duplicate
 in Cards

The type screens offered a handful of actions; they now carry what is
useful in the field for each type, and scroll when they do not fit
(MIFARE Classic has 9). New per type:
- MIFARE Classic: Read NDEF, Magic card: set the UID (csetuid);
- Ultralight/NTAG: Write a page, Read NDEF, Load the dump, Restore, Wipe;
- DESFire: Version, Files of an application (lsfiles), Read a file, Detect
  the key;
- MIFARE Plus: Dump, Read a sector/block, Write a block, MAD, Read NDEF;
- ISO 14443-A: Read NDEF, APDU, Simulate the UID;
- ISO 15693: Write a block, Load, Simulate, Restore;
- iCLASS: Read/Write a block, Load, Simulate;
- T55xx: Info, Read/Write a block, Restore;
- EM4x05: Read/Write a word, Check passwords;
- HITAG: Check keys, Dump, Load, Simulate;
- EM410x/HID/Indala: Simulate and Clone (already added).
Deliberately left out: attacks, magic-card internals beyond the UID, DESFire
app/file management, NDEF writing, value blocks. They stay in the Console.

MIFARE Plus and HITAG dumps now reach Cards (hf-mfp-, lf-hitag-); HITAG
loads and simulates from there.

Cards > a card (list or view) > Duplicate: a second card with its dump
and keys copied to files of their own ("-copyN"), named "<name> copy", so
you can edit or write the copy and keep the original.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 26/26 on the host, incl. test_commands_exist_in_the
_client, which checks every hf/lf command the app types or runs against
the client's own CLIParser definitions (the command exists, each flag is
one of its arguments) -- 60+ commands; Duplicate copies the file and keeps
the type; Plus/HITAG dumps; the type screen scrolls to its last action.
On the badge: the commands on real cards are not yet run.

